# The raw transcripts are not committed. Two reasons, both about what they are
# rather than how big they are -- though they are also ~1MB per role per run:
#
#   * they carry the operator's absolute paths, session ids and home layout
#     verbatim, which is machine state and not a finding;
#   * everything a reader needs is already lifted into RESULT.json -- every
#     failed tool call paired to the command that made it, the trimmed
#     narration, the done_check and its exit code.
#
# A run's stream.jsonl stays on disk where the run wrote it, so re-harvesting an
# old round is a local operation. What travels is the harvest.
evidence/runs/*/*/stream.jsonl
evidence/runs/*/*/stderr.txt
